# Testing Rules

## Always generate (for touched features)

- Unit tests (`LogoDesignPortal.Domain.Tests`, `LogoDesignPortal.Application.Tests`)
- Integration tests (`LogoDesignPortal.API.IntegrationTests`, `[Collection("Integration")]`)
- Playwright E2E (`Frontend/e2e/tests/`)
- Permission / authorization tests (403, 401, role guards)
- Security tests (IDOR, CSRF when cookie auth, upload abuse, webhook signatures)
- Negative tests (invalid input, wrong role, not found)
- Concurrency tests where mutations race (status updates, mark-paid, assign)

## Critical areas (require coverage when changing code)

- Auth (login, cookies, CSRF, refresh, lockout)
- Orders (lifecycle, assign, status API)
- Invoices & payments (client billing, access control)
- Uploads (type, size, duplicate window, visibility)
- SignalR (reconnect, credentials with cookies)
- Role masking (client vs designer DTOs)
- State machine transitions (`OrderStatusStateMachine`, no illegal jumps)

## Never skip

- Unauthorized access (no token, wrong role, other tenant)
- Invalid state transitions
- Edge cases (limits, empty payloads, locked orders)
- Retry / transient failure scenarios where applicable
- Duplicate action tests (double invoice, duplicate upload window)

## Test quality

- **AAA**: Arrange → Act → Assert
- **Deterministic**: no time-of-day flakes; seed via `TestWebApplicationFactory` / factories
- **Isolated**: own `HttpClient` per auth context; in-memory DB per factory instance
- **Production-grade**: assert status codes and bodies; prefer `IntegrationTestJson.Options`; document known gaps in module QA docs under `docs/`

## Project layout

| Layer | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Domain unit | `Backend/src/LogoDesignPortal.Domain.Tests/` |
| Application unit | `Backend/src/LogoDesignPortal.Application.Tests/` |
| API integration | `Backend/src/LogoDesignPortal.API.IntegrationTests/` |
| E2E | `Frontend/e2e/tests/security/`, `workflows/` |
| Module guides | `docs/TESTING_*_MODULE.md`, `docs/QA_*_MODULE.md` |

Do not skip tests in CI. Do not weaken assertions to make flaky tests pass—fix root cause.
